{"format":1,"key":"zone:stranglethorn","path":"/lore/zone/stranglethorn","name":"Stranglethorn Vale","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"stranglethorn","name":"Stranglethorn Vale","path":"/lore/zone/stranglethorn"},"levels":"","description":"Stranglethorn Vale is an untamed, dense jungle dominating the southern tip of the Eastern Kingdoms, south of Duskwood. Once the seat of the great…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:stranglethorn","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Stranglethorn Vale is an untamed, dense jungle dominating the southern tip of the Eastern Kingdoms, south of Duskwood. Once the seat of the great Gurubashi Empire, the rainforest is now strewn with crumbling troll ruins, savage beasts, and competing encampments of goblins, pirates, and soldiers. Control of the region is hotly contested by local troll tribes, the Venture Company, and rival factions carving out footholds in the heat.","For millennia, the vale was governed by the mighty Gurubashi Empire from their capital city, Zul'Gurub. That dominion shattered when radical priests summoned Hakkar the Soulflayer, plunging the region into a catastrophic civil war. Though the Zandalari stepped in to crush the blood god's uprising, the empire splintered beyond repair. Today, the jungle is overrun by warring successor factions—most prominently the Bloodscalp in the northwest and the Skullsplitter in the east—both zealously slaughtering outsiders to reclaim their ancestral home.","Where ancient ruins fall silent, commercial greed fills the void. At the southern tip lies Booty Bay, a bustling haven carved out by the Steamwheedle Cartel and run by the Blackwater Raiders under Baron Revilgaz. The port serves as the prime hub of southern commerce and seafaring transport, though it is perpetually besieged by the rival Bloodsail Buccaneers anchored along the coast. Further inland, the Venture Company aggressively strips the jungle of timber and mines the hills for rare singing crystals.","Stranglethorn Vale serves as one of the most volatile borderlands in the world. The Horde commands Grom'gol Base Camp on the western coast, tethered by goblin zeppelins to Durotar and Tirisfal Glades, while Alliance loyalists operate out of the Rebel Camp to track down the rogue Colonel Kurzen. Amid the dense foliage, the legendary hunter Hemet Nesingwary leads daring big-game expeditions, drawing wanderers into perilous encounters with prowling panthers, enormous apes, and enemy soldiers."],"hash":"754c04","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"77ca08fc57","sec":115},"female-narrator":{"sha":"4979647f0a","sec":121}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Stranglethorn Vale (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Stranglethorn_Vale_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Stranglethorn Vale","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Stranglethorn_Vale"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/booty-bay","n":"Booty Bay","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/grom-gol-base-camp","n":"Grom'gol Base Camp","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/zul-gurub","n":"Zul'Gurub","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/npc/baron-revilgaz","n":"Baron Revilgaz","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/npc/colonel-kurzen","n":"Colonel Kurzen","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/quest/5762-hemet-nesingwary","n":"Hemet Nesingwary","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/nesingwary-s-expedition","n":"Nesingwary's Expedition","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/rebel-camp","n":"Rebel Camp","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/hushed-bank","n":"Hushed Bank","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/vul-gol-ogre-mound","n":"Vul'Gol Ogre Mound","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/quest/1041-the-caravan-road","n":"The Caravan Road","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/item/warsong-axe-shipment","n":"Warsong Axe Shipment","k":"item"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/bal-lal-ruins","n":"Bal'lal Ruins","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/balia-mah-ruins","n":"Balia'mah Ruins","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/booty-bay","n":"Booty Bay","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/cape-of-strangle